      body: '## Overview\n\nA "mining hotel" hosts privately-owned miners in a purpose-built facility \u2014 power, cooling, network, and maintenance handled for a fee while the owner keeps custody and (in the honest model) 100% of payouts. For the heat-reuse community it is the seasonal complement to home heating: run hardware in the house when heat is wanted, hotel it when it is not, or hotel permanently when home electrical capacity, noise, or space forbids.\n\n## The landscape (As-Of 2026-10-11)\n\n- **Abundant Mines** (Oregon) \u2014 "Own the miners, keep 100% of your bitcoin. Full-service hosting at our hydro-powered Oregon facilities. We handle setup, maintenance, and daily operations." \u2014 [capture](../../raw/industry/abundant-mines/2026-10-11-abundant-mines-home.md). Hydro power + full-service is the template: custody stays with the miner, ops go to the hotel.\n- **Hotmine "miner hotel"** \u2014 the Ukrainian pioneer runs "\u0413\u043E\u0442\u0435\u043B\u044C \u0434\u043B\u044F \u043C\u0430\u0439\u043D\u0435\u0440\u0456\u0432" (a hotel for miners) as a store service alongside its heater SKUs \u2014 [capture](../../raw/industry/hotmine/2026-10-11-hotmine-home.md).\n- **Freedomtech.hosting** \u2014 community-built managed model, described by its founder: "The idea of Freedomtech is thats its a combination model of Voltage (everything in the cloud, nothing local, managed for you) and Umbrel/start9 (nothing in the cloud, all local and you are by yourself)." [#970 \xB7 2024-05-19 \xB7 Michael Schmid @Schnitzel] \u2014 i.e., hosted infrastructure with sovereignty retained.\n- **Lincoin** \u2014 named by a pleb planning to host Whatsminers "around August once their new pod is up" [#735 \xB7 2024-04-06 \xB7 Expatriotic] \u2014 community member comparing hosting options by payout-tooling fit.\n\n## What hosting changes (community view)\n\n- The self-hosting objection is technical, not custody: "The argument against self hosted solo mining has always been the worry of stale blocks. But a cloud service could prolly sort out the peering for you." [#969 \xB7 2024-05-19 \xB7 Skot Bitaxe] \u2014 well-run hotels are peers, not landlords.\n- The heat-reuse trade: hosting removes the heat from where you live. Winter argument is home-side ([Air-Cooled Hashrate Heating](../hardware/air-cooled-hashrate-heating.md)); summer or noise-constrained homes push to hotels. No dated anchor quantifies the seasonal hand-off yet \u2014 Phase B candidate.\n\n## Honesty box\n\nNo dated hotel-fee or hosting-rate structure is captured in this repo (firmware "hotel fee" jokes aside \u2014 that is a Vnish/Mujina payout feature, unrelated). Hosting economics remain qualitative here; refresh when an operator publishes terms or the community produces field reports.\n\n## See Also\n\n- [Repair, Supply & Vendors](repair-supply-and-vendors.md)\n- [Hashrate Heating & Mining Infrastructure Companies](hashrate-heating-companies.md)\n- [Community Workshop Wisdom](../getting-started/community-workshop-wisdom.md)'
